{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.AlgebraicQuantumVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.AlgebraicQuantumVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:AlgebraicQuantumVolume.totalVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AlgebraicQuantumVolume.totalVolume","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-quantum-volume.lean#L22-L22","doc":"The product of all traced volumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AlgebraicQuantumVolume.tracedVolume_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AlgebraicQuantumVolume.tracedVolume_pos","kind":"theorem","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-quantum-volume.lean#L20-L20","doc":"Each traced volume is positive for q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AlgebraicQuantumVolume.tracedVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AlgebraicQuantumVolume.tracedVolume","kind":"def","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-quantum-volume.lean#L18-L18","doc":"Traced volume at each level (in ℤ[q^{1/2}, q^{-1/2}]). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AlgebraicQuantumVolume.numCrossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AlgebraicQuantumVolume.numCrossings","kind":"def","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-quantum-volume.lean#L16-L16","doc":"Number of crossings in the braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AlgebraicQuantumVolume.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AlgebraicQuantumVolume.mk","kind":"ctor","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-quantum-volume.lean#L14-L14","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:AlgebraicQuantumVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"AlgebraicQuantumVolume","kind":"structure","line":6,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/algebraic-quantum-volume.lean#L6-L22","doc":"The **algebraic quantum volume** of a braid word β:\nVol_q(β) = ∏ᵢ V̂ᵢ(q) ∈ ℤ[q^{1/2}, q^{-1/2}]\n\nThe product runs over the transfer matrix chain. Each factor\nV̂ᵢ(q) is a traced volume from the i-th level of the brane tower.\n\nThe only transcendental operation is the final logarithm\n(Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm) applied to the algebraic result. ","signatureChunk":0}]}